  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-20T17:14:25.909Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It seems to me a common issue is that people don't know if the person you request on can actually send an invite to you. I've seen a few feature requests that are related to the issue, but I think this one might be the most helpful as it will display the info pro-actively instead of being sent back after a request, thus reducing blind invite requesting.\nAdd a line underneath the receivers status saying if the receiver can or can't invite you depending on the instance type they're in.\nor if no changes to the menu itself can be made, add 2 splash screens stating \"user is in a private world, but can send invites\" and \"user is in a private world and can NOT send invite\" to replace the default \"user is in a private world\" splash screen in the world preview depending on the users relation to the type of instance. (These could also be colour-coded to make it easier to differentiate if need be i.e. green background for can, red backround for can not)\nEither of these will reduce invite requests sent to people who can't invite and might give more socially awkward people more of an incentive to request on people who can as they no longer have the thought \"why bother? They probably can't invite me anyway\" stopping them from trying.",
